      "claim_id": "memory-command-execution-model",
      "text": "Redis official benchmark documentation describes Redis as an in-memory data store and, from the point of view of command execution, mostly single-threaded while modern Redis versions use threads for different work; official latency guidance describes client requests as sequentially served using multiplexing.",
