    {
      "claim_id": "pipeline-rtt-syscall-and-buffer-tradeoff",
      "text": "Redis official pipelining documentation explains that clients can send multiple commands without waiting for each reply, reducing per-command RTT and allowing multiple commands/replies to share read/write system calls; it also warns that the server queues replies in memory and recommends bounded batches for large pipelines.",
      "source_ids": [
        "redis-pipelining"
